;; The channels of OCaml's runtime (runtime/io.c, runtime/caml/io.h): a buffered file descriptor
;; with the C runtime's exact buffering, so that what reaches the descriptor, and when, is what
;; OCaml's runtime does. The interpreter's lock serialises the channels, so they need no mutex.


